@comparison-numerical-v1
Feature: EN 1995 structural scene
  The timber snapshot and its check report project to a deterministic, locale-free 3D scene, a set of 2D diagrams and drag handles.

  Further specification assertions, asserted by the Rust unit tests of the crate and not by the platform adapters:
  - glulam members extrude their section in lamellae: Given the compliant glulam floor beam When the scene is projected Then entity "beam-B1" is a member of 5.00 m whose section area equals width times depth
  - utilisation colours the governing entity: Given the compliant glulam floor beam and its check report When the scene is projected Then entity "beam-B1" carries the largest utilisation of its checks And a failing member in the overloaded building has error style, a diagonal hatch and a failure glyph
  - fire shows the char layer and the zero-strength layer: Given the compliant glulam floor beam burning for 30 minutes When the scene is projected Then entity "beam-B1" has the residual section of the effective charring depth And entities "beam-B1:char" and "beam-B1:zsl" are hulls whose areas follow the char depth and the effective depth
  - connections show the fastener grid and the spacing zones: Given the compliant bolt group When the scene is projected Then entity "conn-C1:fasteners" is a grid of rows by fasteners per row with the spacing a1 and the minimum a2 And the spacing zones are coloured by their own spacing check
  - floors show the vibration mode: Given the compliant glulam floor beam When the scene is projected Then entity "beam-B1" carries the first eigen-mode of the mechanics kernel for its support, equal to pi / (2 L^2) sqrt(EI / m) within 0.2 % for a pinned beam, antisymmetric about the middle support for two spans
  - handles write document leaves: Given the compliant glulam floor beam When the span handle of "beam-B1" is dragged to 5.012 m Then one write sets "members[id=beam-B1].spanM" to 5.0 m And the notch and fire handles invert to the current values
  - diagrams agree with the closed forms: Given the compliant glulam floor beam and its bolt group When the diagrams are built Then the k_c markers lie on the buckling curve and the Johansen governing bar is the lowest And an independent Python oracle reproduces the section areas, the k_c and k_crit curves, the failure modes and the char hulls
  - check stations colour the member, the deformed shape and every fastener: Given the compliant glulam floor beam and its bolt group When the check engine evaluates the structure Then bending, shear, tension, combined and the three deflection checks carry 11 stations along the length whose maximum is the check utilisation And the fire check carries 11 stations of the field "fire-time" with the effective char depth And the Johansen check carries one station per fastener of the field "fastener-force" whose largest force is F_Ed / n_ef And the member binding is the envelope of those stations, the deformed shape samples the final-deflection stations and the fastener entity is tinted per instance
  - the fire time track grows the char layer with the charring rate: Given a timber member burning for <minutes> minutes with the one-dimensional charring rate beta_n When the fire track is scrubbed to that duration Then the char layer of the keyframe has the area b h - (b - 2 beta_n t)(h - 2 beta_n t) Examples (4 rows: 30, 60, 90, 120)
  - The fastener field shows its effective number, splitting plane and row shear block: Given a committed connection with a row of fasteners along the grain When the structural scene and its diagrams are projected Then the n_ef diagram equals the effective number of EN 1995-1-1 8.3.1.1 or 8.5.1.1 and drags the number of fasteners And the connection holds a splitting plane along the grain and a translucent row shear block over the fastener field
  - Annex B and C, fire and bridge cases are drawn with handles and diagrams that have table twins: Given a document case of entry <entry> with the committed inputs of the catalogue fixture When the structural scene, its handles and its diagrams are projected Then the scene contains the entity <entity> and the diagram <diagram> has a table twin And every handle writes a leaf of the case in the unit of the input vocabulary Examples (7 rows: t-90-part1-case-gamma, t-93-spacer0-0-case-column, t-106-residual-case-fire-reduced, t-107-char-60-case-clt-fire, t-121-block1-case-sn, t-122-laminations-case-prestress, t-120-crowd-case-crowd)
  - The zero direction of an angular handle is the projected +X axis: Given a tapered and a curved pitched beam case with their angle handles When the anchor of each angular handle is measured about its axis from the projected +X axis Then the affine map of the handle returns the document angle in degrees and the angle lies inside the limits of the handle
  - tapers and cutouts have a grip on every numeric geometric field: Given a document with a double tapered member with rods, a single tapered member, a notch with rods and a hole When the grips of each entity are built Then every geometric field (taper angle, apex depth, inner radius, lamella thickness, apex angle, notch depth, notch length, notch distance, notch slope, hole diameter, position and height, rod count) has a grip that writes the stored field in metres, radians or counts and whose anchor reads back the current value And the notch void is as long as the notch length
  - entity curves follow the checks: Given the same document When the diagrams are built Then the single tapered beam shows the tapered and the parallel edge utilisation along its span for the moment line of its load case (the highest point of the curve equals the check utilisation and carries the governing-section marker, left of midspan for a uniform load on a beam that deepens towards the far support) with the marker on the member span, the notch shows k_v and the shear utilisation over its depth with the limit 1, the reinforced notch and the apex the tension utilisation over the depth and the rod count, the apex k_l, k_r and k_p over the inner radius and the hole the net-section utilisation over its diameter with the 0.15 h limit And every marker writes an entity field and an independent Python oracle reproduces k_v, k_l, k_p, k_r and the notch tension force
  - every check of the spec trace is bound: Given the spec trace of EN 1995 When the scene and the diagrams of the fixtures are built Then each check id has one registry row with its entity collection and diagram key And every entity that carries the check has a utilisation-coloured 3D body and its diagram has a marker bound to the check
